**Issue**: #316
**Date**: 2026-08-28
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

@issue-316 @start-issue @bug
Feature: Reuse existing issue branches during start
  The start controller must reuse the exact canonical issue branch before attempting to create it.

  Scenario: Reuse a local canonical issue branch
    Given the repository is clean on another branch
    And the canonical issue branch exists locally
    When the start controller prepares the issue
    Then it checks out the local canonical issue branch
    And it does not create a GitHub development branch

  Scenario: Reuse an origin canonical issue branch
    Given the repository is clean on another branch
    And the canonical issue branch does not exist locally
    And the exact canonical issue branch exists on origin
    When the start controller prepares the issue
    Then it fetches the exact origin branch
    And it creates a local branch tracking that origin branch
    And it does not create a GitHub development branch

  Scenario: Create a missing canonical issue branch
    Given the repository is clean on another branch
    And the canonical issue branch does not exist locally or on origin
    When the start controller prepares the issue
    Then it creates and checks out the canonical GitHub development branch

  Scenario: Fail closed when checkout does not activate the canonical branch
    Given a canonical branch path was selected
    And checkout does not leave the canonical branch active
    When the start controller verifies the branch
    Then the start handoff fails with reason code branch_checkout_failed
    And no user work is reset, stashed, forced, or discarded
